Z||000000||mrgone||06-17-2001||10:22 PM||||i get stinky blue smoke when i start my car<BR>its idleing pretty rough too...<BR>the needle doesnt bounce when it idles though<BR>but sometimes if i hammer it in nuetral it takes a needel a split second like the car abruptley shunted into a high rpm rage<P>still have my iac (idle air control) valve problem too<BR>i dont know how well this car will last it needs alot of work. has high milage too.<BR> im a student and i take a carpool to work, so its really just my toy grocery getter and i like driving.||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||06-17-2001||10:37 PM||||blue smoke on start is most often failed valve seals. Kind of a minor problem.<P>rough idle can be a number of things. check all the vacuum lines/fittngs/etc and check timing if it is a distributor motor.<P>Also, unplug the "tach filter" and see if it idles better. that will kill the tach on the dash but won't otherwise effect engine operation. (Unless the thing is bad in what case it will run better.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||06-18-2001||09:15 AM||||You are burning oil from the worn valve seals. So have you looked at the plugs to be sure they aren't fouled? Rough idle could result from that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||06-18-2001||01:08 PM||||almost everyone i know with a V6 has the problem to some extent. Mine does it every once in a while, but only for a second. ever since it was new. still runs fine after 86K||||reg||1
